comments.body:
@Alison Pill - As a mom of young adult twins, and watching them grow up on Disney and Nickelodeon shows always made me wonder how those young actors managed such intense fame. For those who stayed in Hollywood, it must be incredible pressure. Life's daily stress is hard enough without living it in a fishbowl.
I appreciate your point about Greta Gerwig’s Little Women. Utilizing adult actors rather than casting scenes with children shows that you don't always need real child actors to depict growing up—a choice that honors important boundaries on set while granting the audience a meaningful moment of suspended disbelief.
Best of luck to you in your future endeavors!
